{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117148","id":3364173463,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7IhTaX","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117148","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117148.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117148.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117148","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117148/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117148/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117148/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e16a299a867a2230fde22c7ee4d7b85c9bcbeca9","number":117148,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Raytracing API adjustments.","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I've made several experimental changes to the raytracing API to address some potential pitfalls I'm concerned about.\r\n\r\n## Acceleration structure instances\r\n\r\nI added an acceleration structure instance struct that maps directly to the instance descriptors used in D3D12/Vulkan/Metal. The only missing part is the hit group index, which will need to be addressed later. Previously, only the BLAS and the transform could be specified.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nenum AccelerationStructureInstanceFlagBits {\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INSTANCE_TRIANGLE_FACING_CULL_DISABLE_BIT = (1 << 0),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INSTANCE_TRIANGLE_FLIP_FACING_BIT = (1 << 1),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INSTANCE_FORCE_OPAQUE_BIT = (1 << 2),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INSTANCE_FORCE_NO_OPAQUE_BIT = (1 << 3),\r\n};\r\n\r\nstruct AccelerationStructureInstance {\r\n\tTransform3D transform;\r\n\tuint32_t id = 0;\r\n\tuint8_t mask = 0xFF;\r\n\tBitField<AccelerationStructureInstanceFlagBits> flags = {};\r\n\tRID blas;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Acceleration structure flags\r\n\r\nThese map directly to the flags available in D3D12/Vulkan/Metal. Previously, the Vulkan backend always forced fast trace bit, which is not ideal for animated models.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nenum AccelerationStructureFlagBits {\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_ALLOW_UPDATE_BIT = (1 << 0),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_ALLOW_COMPACTION_BIT = (1 << 1),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_PREFER_FAST_TRACE_BIT = (1 << 2),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_PREFER_FAST_BUILD_BIT = (1 << 3),\r\n\tACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_LOW_MEMORY_BIT = (1 << 4),\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n## TLAS instances buffer\r\n\r\nI removed this API. Apparently, the idea behind exposing it was to allow the GPU to populate the instance buffer directly: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99119#discussion_r1987836073\r\n\r\nI don't really see a way for this to work correctly:\r\n- The instance descriptor layout differs on Metal.\r\n- There is no way to track which BLASes are referenced inside the buffer.\r\n\r\nWhile I will not be implementing it in this PR, I have a possible alternative design:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n// The GPU side struct.\r\nstruct AccelerationStructureIndirectInstance {\r\n\tTransform3D transform;\r\n\tuint32_t id = 0;\r\n\tuint8_t mask = 0xFF;\r\n    uint32_t reserved = 0; // Reserved for future hit group index.\r\n\tBitField<AccelerationStructureInstanceFlagBits> flags = {};\r\n\tuint32_t blas_index = 0;\r\n};\r\n\r\nstruct AccelerationStructureIndirectInstanceBuffer {\r\n    RID buffer;\r\n    uint32_t offset = 0;\r\n    uint32_t count = 0;\r\n    Span<RID> blases;\r\n};\r\n\r\nError tlas_build(RID p_tlas, Span<AccelerationStructureInstance> p_instances, Span<AccelerationStructureIndirectInstanceBuffer> p_indirect_instance_buffers);\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsers can provide buffers following the struct layout defined by Godot. Internally, the graphics backend would run a compute shader to translate this layout into the backend specific instance format.\r\n\r\nSince BLAS references would also index into the CPU provided BLAS list, the engine would be able to track them correctly.\r\n\r\nThe instance buffer also had a race condition where it could be written to while the previous frame was using it to build the TLAS. I changed it to create multiple internal instance buffers unique to every frame.\r\n\r\n## Draw tracker management\r\n\r\nThe previous implementation did not work correctly.\r\n\r\nI replaced it with an implementation that creates weak links between TLASes and BLASes. When a BLAS is rebuilt or freed, any TLAS that referenced it is invalidated and must be rebuilt. In practice, this should be fine since TLASes rarely remain static between frames and typically need rebuilding anyway.\r\n\r\nThe weak link preserves the TLAS object's internal memory and avoids destroying uniform sets that depend on it. If a hard dependency were added through `_add_dependency`, any BLAS modification would destroy the TLAS object entirely, and uniform sets that depend on it.\r\n\r\nTo detect invalid states, I added error checks that trigger when:\r\n- BLASes are provided in TLAS build despite requiring rebuilding.\r\n- TLASes are bound through uniform sets despite requiring rebuilding.\r\n\r\nBLASes should also ideally be invalidated if any write operations occur on the buffers they depend on, but this is not implemented yet.\r\n\r\n## Acceleration structure build input usage\r\n\r\nI removed this. It was used for both BLASes and vertex/index buffers, which is incorrect. Buffer inputs in BLAS need `VK_ACCESS_SHADER_READ_BIT`, which maps to `RESOURCE_USAGE_STORAGE_BUFFER_READ`.\r\n\r\n## To Do\r\n- [x] Documentation.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gis